        "reference": "Job 3:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And Job spake, and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the day perish wherein I was born, and the night in which it was said, There is a man child conceived.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Despair."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Jer. 20:14 (14–18)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Despair.",
            "prettyString": "TG Despair",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Despair",
                "entryId": "tg-despair",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Let that day be darkness; let not God regard it from above, neither let the light shine upon it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Let darkness and the shadow of death stain it; let a cloud dwell upon it; let the blackness of the day terrify it.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "Ps. 23:4; 44:19; 107:14 (10, 14); D&C 57:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "As for that night, let darkness seize upon it; let it not be joined unto the days of the year, let it not come into the number of the months.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Lo, let that night be solitary, let no joyful voice come therein.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Let them curse it that curse the day, who are ready to raise up their mourning.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark; let it look for light, but have none; neither let it see the dawning of the day:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "Because it shut not up the doors of my mother’s womb, nor hid sorrow from mine eyes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Why died I not from the womb? why did I not give up the ghost when I came out of the belly?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "Job 10:18 (18–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Why did the knees prevent me? or why the breasts that I should suck?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "HEB receive."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "For now should I have lain still and been quiet, I should have slept: then had I been at rest,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built desolate places for themselves;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "HEB who rebuilt ruins."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Or with princes that had gold, who filled their houses with silver:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Or as an hidden untimely birth I had not been; as infants which never saw light.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:16",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "There the wicked cease from troubling; and there the weary be at rest.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Paradise."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Paradise.",
            "prettyString": "TG Paradise",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Paradise",
                "entryId": "tg-paradise",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:17",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "There the prisoners rest together; they hear not the voice of the oppressor.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:18",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "The small and great are there; and the servant is free from his master.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:19",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery, and life unto the bitter in soul;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "D&C 88:67."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "D&C 122:7 (1–7). TG Suffering."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "D&C 88:67.",
            "prettyString": "D&C 88:67",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
