                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:21",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Which rejoice exceedingly, and are glad, when they can find the grave?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:22",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Why is light given to a man whose way is hid, and whom God hath hedged in?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:23",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "For my sighing cometh before I eat, and my roarings are poured out like the waters.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:24",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "For the thing which I greatly feared is come upon me, and that which I was afraid of is come unto me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 3:25",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "I was not in safety, neither had I rest, neither was I quiet; yet trouble came.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
